+"""Solute-driven motion of a freely suspended sphere.
+
+The apparatus is described in ``README.md``.  The only unknown material
+property is the uniform dynamic viscosity; every other quantity is either a
+known input (``radius``, ``width``, ``strength``, ``slip``) or a fixed
+instrument constant.
+
+``response`` returns the *reduced* signed response
+
+    value = response(radius, width, strength, slip) / viscosity,
+
+i.e. the sphere velocity per unit imposed concentration gradient ``G``.  The
+reduced response is obtained by solving the steady solute-transport problem
+around the sphere and folding the resulting solute force into the creeping-flow
+hydrodynamic mobility of the sphere.
